Oh that wasn't a bad game. Hope that it didn't leave a bones level though.

If you get a chance go and read that other thread. My take on your game is
that you levelled up too fast without securing sufficient AC to take on
the monsters you were coming across. Some tips.

1) You did good by keeping the cat around. Grow the pet and let them help
you.

2) The cloak of displacement would have been helpful. You may have skipped
a couple of those initial hits.

3) Levelling up has its benefits and its costs. The soldier ants and the
leocrotta were direct results of your high XL.

4) Did you clean out the shops? Goods and money are good things.

5) If you would like a first target, take a read on posts I've made recently
on the MineTown Protection Run. It'll give you some more defensive skills tips,
some thoughts on levelling up, cleaning out shops, buffing the pet (which you
did), and more sure early game managment.

Keep playing, next time you'll get an early wish. Remember that a wizard should
spend it on silver dragon scale mail.

Good luck.

